/// `exact-amplitudes`: Exact Clifford+T amplitudes in ℤ[1/√2, i].
/// Implemented: an amplitude stands at its least scale, so equal amplitudes have equal forms. Its sums, products, negations, conjugates and squared moduli are exact, and the gates `H`, `S` and `T` act on the state of one qubit.
/// Not implemented: no measurement gives the exact weights of the Born rule for a state.
///
/// - owes: #5742
// A product of two amplitudes reduces to the least scale. Thus `ω · ω` is
// `i` at the scale zero, and `(1/√2) · (1/√2)` is one half, exact at the
// scale one. The model exemplar runs a whole circuit.
//
// - see: `../../model/quantum/amplitudes.gandr`

// The exact amplitudes and their product.
import std.quantum (Amplitude, omega, sqrtHalf, times);

/// `ω · ω = i`, at the scale zero.
@[ runs("Amp 0 0 1 0 Whole") ]
def phase() -> Amplitude { times omega omega }

/// `(1/√2) · (1/√2) = 1/2`, at the scale one.
@[ runs("Amp 1 0 0 0 (Halved Whole)") ]
def half() -> Amplitude { times sqrtHalf sqrtHalf }
